&gt;&gt;&gt; Optimal	Hospitals, Tools (non-bladed)
&gt;&gt; Suitable	Light/Thermal Armor
X Inadvisable 	Production

Tools Recommended: Any non-bladed
Notes: Corrosion-resistant, Superalloy, Light

Also known as Ti-6Al-4V or more commonly Grade 5 Titanium, it's alloyed with Aluminium and Vanadium. Due to its strength, light weight, and shock-absorbing qualities, it makes fine tools (especially non-bladed ones). And being a superalloy along with Stellite, Pyromet, and Nimonic, it's useful for high-temperature applications and components, and makes lightweight and decently strong armor with a nearly unmatched in energy-weapon defense rating (among alloy armors). It's extremely hard to work with, however.</description>
